<title>FRANCE: IHT says in printing alliance with Wattachak.</title>
<headline>IHT says in printing alliance with Wattachak.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Herald Tribune said on Thursday it has formed a strategic alliance with Thai media and publishing company the Wattachak Group to print the newspaper in Bangkok, Thailand.</p>
<p>Richard McClean, chief executive and publisher of the International Herald Tribune said in a statement &quot;Adding this new printing facility to the existing 12 sites the International Herald Tribune already has around the world is the first step of a renewed expansion program for the newspaper from its headquarters in Paris, France.&quot;</p>
<p>The International Herald Tribune is co-owned by the New York Times and the Washington Post.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
